// XFAIL: RT-31b: a loan of a static's place is live at every point (solve.vl, D6.2.5), so a later move out of the static is also reported as a move of a borrowed place (borrowck.move_borrowed); rustc tracks no loan of a static (a borrow through its `&'static` is ignore_borrow) and gives the E0507 alone (open)
// RULE: M3, D6.2.5
// (0.30.1, open) A static borrowed, the borrow's last use, then a move out
// of the static: rustc gives one error, E0507 "cannot move out of `SW.d` as
// `SW` is a static item" at 24:13, nothing about the borrow (a `let r =
// &SW;` used before the move is the same).
// ERROR: error[borrowck.move_out]: cannot move out of 'SW.d', a static
// ERROR: line 24, column 13
// ERROR-COUNT: 1
struct D {
    v: i64,
}

struct W {
    d: D,
}

static SW: W = W { d: D { v: 2 } };

fn main() {
    match &SW {
        W { d } => println("{}", d.v),
    }
    let u = SW.d;
    println("{}", u.v);
}
